---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Discover actual command declarations or lazily query one argument's candidates

Usage: pse commands [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...  Select a command path below pse; absence selects the root

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --json
      --format <FORMAT>      Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --markdown             Publish Markdown directly from the owning parser, without candidate acquisition
      --argument <ARGUMENT>  Query candidates for this argument ID or long option, rather than command descriptions
      --fields <FIELDS>      Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage
      --budget <BUDGET>      Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --prefix <PREFIX>      [default: ""]
      --offset <OFFSET>      [default: 0]
      --limit <LIMIT>
      --metadata <METADATA>  Explicit retained Cargo metadata; only a selected metadata provider reads it
  -h, --help                 Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Discover actual command declarations or lazily query one argument's candidates

Usage: pse commands [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...
          Select a command path below pse; absence selects the root

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --json


      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --markdown
          Publish Markdown directly from the owning parser, without candidate acquisition

      --argument <ARGUMENT>
          Query candidates for this argument ID or long option, rather than command descriptions

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --prefix <PREFIX>
          [default: ""]

      --offset <OFFSET>
          [default: 0]

      --limit <LIMIT>


      --metadata <METADATA>
          Explicit retained Cargo metadata; only a selected metadata provider reads it

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
